05903053, 0.05458666384220123, -0.026963811367750168, 0.12391279637813568, 0.08409199118614197, 0.04704156890511513, -0.006318208295851946, 0.06116480380296707, -0.06272371858358383, -0.014568335376679897, -0.0011882161488756537, -0.02349417842924595, 0.0224557314068079, -0.024996154010295868, 0.007338959723711014, -0.0331166610121727, 0.0170272309333086, -0.030055765062570572, 0.029928267002105713, 0.046139802783727646, 0.023121152073144913, -0.024419395253062248, -0.1356373280286789, -0.017917387187480927, 0.022971654310822487, 0.08576972037553787, 0.021792825311422348, -0.06530933082103729, -0.07413077354431152, 0.021371282637119293, 0.07839184254407883, -0.04620705544948578, 0.006636560894548893, 0.07529710978269577, -0.02758357673883438, -0.06357627362012863, -0.015628652647137642]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWe\u2019re working within the shared range [-10, 10]. To establish a neutral baseline and gauge everyone\u2019s preferences, I propose starting at <VALUE> 0 </VALUE>. From here, we can adjust incrementally toward a stable, balanced choice.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "\nA small step downward stays within safe bounds and helps us gauge alignment without overcommitting. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "\nA modest move back toward the neutral baseline keeps things balanced while we gauge comfort. This slight upward step should remain reasonable for the group. <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s be more decisive and move away from the neutral baseline to learn where preferences truly lie. A slightly bolder step remains safe while clarifying commitments. <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "\nMomentum favors a decisive move away from neutrality to test comfort with a stronger stance. I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE> to clarify whether larger magnitude is acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s reduce instability from an overly negative stance with a careful upward adjustment that preserves momentum. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a careful step back toward center to test comfort while staying conservative. This should keep things reasonable as we gauge upward tolerance. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious midpoint between recent positions reduces risk while keeping us near center. Let\u2019s test comfort at <VALUE>-2</VALUE> before any further shifts.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "\nA small, measured step toward center improves stability and tests positive tolerance without overshooting. <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "\nCenter drift isn\u2019t informative. Let\u2019s commit to a clearer stance by testing a stronger positive. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "\nSplitting the difference between 2 and 4 should yield a more robust balance without overextending. Let\u2019s test <VALUE>3</VALUE> to check comfort while keeping positive momentum.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "\nCenter drift isn\u2019t informative\u2014let\u2019s commit to a clearer stance. <VALUE>5</VALUE> This tests tolerance for firmer positive momentum.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid overextending, let\u2019s make a cautious correction that still tests positive tolerance.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a modest step up to keep positive momentum without overextending. This splits the difference between recent positions and should be broadly acceptable.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "b671acd3-59e1-438b-9819-a1730f9568f0"}, {"answer": "\nTo ground the discussion, let\u2019s confirm the shared range is [-10, 10]. As a neutral baseline to assess stability and trade-offs, I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE> and suggest we adjust incrementally based on everyone\u2019s feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "The baseline feels overly cautious; let\u2019s take a modest but clearer step away from zero.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis tests stability while signaling commitment without overreaching.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "\nA small nudge upward seems safe given the last move\u2019s stability; let\u2019s test whether a modest increase still aligns for everyone.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "\nA small downward step reduces risk while staying aligned with prior modest moves. It\u2019s a cautious compromise to test convergence without overcommitting upward.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019ve hovered in a timid range; let\u2019s be more decisive while staying within a stable step. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward nudge keeps us close to the recent center while responding to calls for decisiveness.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf this feels too brisk, we can revert slightly after hearing reactions.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "\nBuilding on the recent upward lean, let\u2019s commit to a bolder yet controlled move to test decisiveness.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "\nDecisive yet controlled step from 2 to test commitment while staying close to consensus. <VALUE>4</VALUE> If that feels too brisk, we can reassess at 3.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "\nThis stays close to where we\u2019ve been and probes alignment. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "\nTo preserve robustness and balance, let\u2019s take a measured step back toward the stable middle. This keeps momentum while staying aligned with recent signals.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "72b168b6-993d-4c78-addb-e22424f1f2ad"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s confirm we\u2019re choosing an integer x within the shared range [-10, 10]. To begin, I suggest a neutral baseline <VALUE> 0 </VALUE> so we can test fit and adjust in small steps toward a stable, balanced design.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "d35b2b3c-4d25-46b3-8ab7-5d18dd2da941"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward move keeps us close to center and lets us gauge comfort near mildly higher values. Proposed: <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "d35b2b3c-4d25-46b3-8ab7-5d18dd2da941"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s try a modest uptick to probe stability near the low positive region.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nWe can adjust by a small step if this isn\u2019t comfortable.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "d35b2b3c-4d25-46b3-8ab7-5d18dd2da941"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "d35b2b3c-4d25-46b3-8ab7-5d18dd2da941"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "d35b2b3c-4d25-46b3-8ab7-5d18dd2da941"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019ve tested 3; let\u2019s verify robustness by stepping slightly lower to see if comfort improves.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "d35b2b3c-4d25-46b3-8ab7-5d18dd2da941"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down helps avoid unnecessary risk and tests comfort nearer the safer side. Proposed: <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "d35b2b3c-4d25-46b3-8ab7-5d18dd2da941"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s be more decisive and probe the upper side where co